WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.330
Around 1190, in Old Cairo, a court physician
finished a book for a Jew torn between

2
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:08.220
Torah and reason.

3
00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:13.490
The physician was Maimonides, who
was also a rabbi and a philosopher.

4
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:18.730
Today, some people feel that science
replaces wonder with explanation.

5
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:24.050
So can studying the stars and the cells
of the body be a way of loving God?

6
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.430
In this mission, you'll
meet his three great works:

7
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:31.530
a commentary, a code of law
and a book of philosophy.

8
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.830
Then you'll read his
answer to an old question:

9
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.800
how does a person come to love God?

10
00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:41.080
Your mission: find out
whether, for Maimonides,

11
00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:45.090
studying the stars and the body
can be a way of loving God.
